WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:03.319
In this part of our level editing,

2
00:00:03.319 --> 00:00:05.519
I want to talk about landscape patches.

3
00:00:05.519 --> 00:00:07.960
Now, landscape patches are a really great way

4
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:12.039
to define how the landscape will

5
00:00:12.039 --> 00:00:15.800
be affected when a certain actor or group of actors

6
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.679
is placed in the level.

7
00:00:18.679 --> 00:00:21.280
In the scene in front of us, we have an example of the two

8
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.039
types of patches that we have available.

9
00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:25.960
We have a texture patch and a circle patch.

10
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.760
And the difference between them is this.

11
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.140
The texture patch allows us a much finer control

12
00:00:30.179 --> 00:00:32.579
over how the surface is going to be affected.

13
00:00:32.579 --> 00:00:34.380
In fact, in this example, what we're actually

14
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.460
using here is the crater texture

15
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:43.280
that was utilized in the landscape sculpting example.

16
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.280
And over on the right, you can see the circle height patch.

17
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.840
And this is just using a procedural circle

18
00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.920
with a procedural falloff.

19
00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.880
And you can see what it's having

20
00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.560
an effect on the landscape.

21
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.799
Now, to work with this, it's very, very simple.

22
00:00:56.799 --> 00:01:01.420
All we need to do is simply select the static mesh

23
00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.740
or group of static mesh or actor

24
00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:05.099
that's placed in the world.

25
00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:07.540
And we can then click on Add.

26
00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.780
And from the Add menu, we can add the landscape circle height

27
00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.019
patch component or the landscape texture patch

28
00:01:15.019 --> 00:01:15.620
component.

29
00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.459
Once we've done that, the first time we're

30
00:01:17.459 --> 00:01:18.939
going to be asked where we want

31
00:01:18.939 --> 00:01:20.939
to insert this new edit layer.

32
00:01:20.939 --> 00:01:24.019
And we do need a landscape patches edit layer.

33
00:01:24.019 --> 00:01:26.060
And once we've done that, we will then

34
00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.620
be able to adjust the settings.

35
00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.739
And first things first, we do need to select the landscape.

36
00:01:30.739 --> 00:01:34.019
So inside of either the circle height patch or the texture

37
00:01:34.019 --> 00:01:35.540
patch, we do need to make sure

38
00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:36.980
that landscape is selected.

39
00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:38.340
And the best way to do this is

40
00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:41.540
to simply click on the menu showing the landscape

41
00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.620
and then selecting it.

42
00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.420
Let's go ahead and pop over to the editor

43
00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:45.939
and see how this works.

44
00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:48.980
So first off, what we're going to do is right here,

45
00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:51.980
I have just a very simple this floor right here,

46
00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.659
which is right at the bottom of this.

47
00:01:53.659 --> 00:01:54.939
I'm going to come here and add.

48
00:01:54.939 --> 00:01:57.459
And we're just going to look for our L-A-N-D.

49
00:01:57.459 --> 00:01:59.459
And there is our landscape circle height.

50
00:01:59.459 --> 00:02:01.340
So notice again, nothing happened.

51
00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.340
So I'm just going to come here and click

52
00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:05.099
on my landscape.

53
00:02:05.099 --> 00:02:07.939
And let's go ahead and kind of move this out a little bit.

54
00:02:07.939 --> 00:02:08.500
There we go.

55
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.620
Whoops, made it a little bit too wide.

56
00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.219
And maybe make this fall off a little bit more.

57
00:02:13.219 --> 00:02:13.979
There we go.

58
00:02:13.979 --> 00:02:16.580
The other thing we can do is with this selected,

59
00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.860
we can actually move it up and down.

60
00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.020
So that we can have something like that.

61
00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.099
There we go.

62
00:02:24.099 --> 00:02:28.099
Now, if we were to take all of these things together

63
00:02:28.099 --> 00:02:34.110
and then put them into a level, create packed level

64
00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:36.430
actor with all of this, when we bring that out,

65
00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:40.069
it'll be able to do this really interesting offset

66
00:02:40.069 --> 00:02:41.430
to the landscape.

67
00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:44.990
So let's go ahead and we're going to come here.

68
00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:47.509
And it's this brick right around here somewhere.

69
00:02:47.509 --> 00:02:48.590
I believe it's this one.

70
00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:49.310
So there we go.

71
00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:51.229
So let's just delete this for the time being.

72
00:02:51.229 --> 00:02:52.550
So we're going to delete that.

73
00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:55.629
And let's come here to our land.

74
00:02:55.629 --> 00:02:58.009
And we're going to add the texture patch.

75
00:02:58.009 --> 00:02:58.669
So there we go.

76
00:02:58.669 --> 00:02:59.710
So there's our texture patch.

77
00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:02.349
And again, texture patch is going to look quite different.

78
00:03:02.349 --> 00:03:04.870
So first off, let's make sure we get our landscape going

79
00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.030
on in there.

80
00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:12.129
And we can come here to our source mode.

81
00:03:12.129 --> 00:03:15.129
And we can change this to, say, a texture asset.

82
00:03:15.129 --> 00:03:17.409
And then I'm going to hit Control Space here.

83
00:03:17.409 --> 00:03:19.449
We're going to look for our brushes.

84
00:03:19.449 --> 00:03:21.530
We're going to take this impact graders.

85
00:03:21.569 --> 00:03:23.229
And we can use that as our texture asset.

86
00:03:23.229 --> 00:03:23.889
So there we go.

87
00:03:23.889 --> 00:03:28.580
We are actually going to be offsetting by that.

88
00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.819
We can then also reinitialize the height

89
00:03:31.819 --> 00:03:34.939
to make sure that it's actually sitting on the right location.

90
00:03:34.939 --> 00:03:43.909
And let's just set this to maybe like 3 by 3.

91
00:03:43.909 --> 00:03:45.360
There we go.

92
00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:51.389
And we might want to just bring it this way a little bit more.

93
00:03:51.389 --> 00:03:53.870
And we're not getting a really good result here.

94
00:03:53.870 --> 00:04:02.639
So let's go ahead and we can try adjusting the blend mode.

95
00:04:02.639 --> 00:04:05.159
Let's see if Min will give us one.

96
00:04:05.159 --> 00:04:07.840
Oops, and I didn't mean to do that.

97
00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.479
So I'm going to hit Control Z. Let's just try Max.

98
00:04:10.479 --> 00:04:12.120
And this is just affecting the way

99
00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:17.290
that the texture here is going to be placed over the top.

100
00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.889
And I'm just trying to find one that is going

101
00:04:19.889 --> 00:04:26.480
to give me a little bit better.

102
00:04:26.519 --> 00:04:27.560
Let's try our 0 to 1.

103
00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.040
There we go.

104
00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:28.839
That's what it was.

105
00:04:28.839 --> 00:04:29.639
It was our 0 to 1.

106
00:04:29.639 --> 00:04:31.199
A little bit better encoding so I can actually

107
00:04:31.199 --> 00:04:33.120
see what's going on inside of the landscape.

108
00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.279
And it was setting our 0 to 1 right there.

109
00:04:35.279 --> 00:04:39.240
So we can also, I believe, change

110
00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.959
this to give us a little bit more depth

111
00:04:42.959 --> 00:04:44.040
inside of our landscape.

112
00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:47.149
Oh, just there we go.

113
00:04:47.149 --> 00:04:49.430
So you can see here that's actually affecting it

114
00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.870
and adding those craters in there.

115
00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:55.589
Remember, the landscape doesn't have too crazy amount

116
00:04:55.589 --> 00:04:56.509
of tessellation.

117
00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:58.230
We do have displacement available.

118
00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:01.110
The actual individual landscape quads

119
00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.350
are not super, super, super big.

120
00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:07.110
So that's why sometimes this, whoops, and I set that up.

121
00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.350
I want to keep that at 0.5.

122
00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:11.990
So that's why sometimes we'll get these errors like this

123
00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:15.029
is that if we just come here and we go to our wireframe,

124
00:05:15.029 --> 00:05:20.100
remember, we don't have a crazy amount of detail

125
00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:20.720
right here.

126
00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.319
So just keep that in mind as you

127
00:05:22.319 --> 00:05:26.480
are building this that oftentimes these foundations

128
00:05:26.519 --> 00:05:28.959
are really going to work best when you have something that

129
00:05:28.959 --> 00:05:33.120
is maybe more similar to, let's come back over here

130
00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.199
to this twin mountain, to the mountain, I should say,

131
00:05:36.199 --> 00:05:37.959
example.

132
00:05:37.959 --> 00:05:40.120
And we're probably going to have to make this thing

133
00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:43.420
really, really, really huge.

134
00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:44.259
Yeah, there we go.

135
00:05:44.259 --> 00:05:45.740
We got a little bit of fall off.

136
00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.500
And then we probably need to like,

137
00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:52.829
we could multiply this by 4 and multiply this one by 4.

138
00:05:52.829 --> 00:05:53.509
There we go.

139
00:05:53.509 --> 00:05:54.470
Something like that.

140
00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:58.149
And then we would need to adjust the height of it

141
00:05:58.149 --> 00:05:59.149
accordingly.

142
00:05:59.149 --> 00:06:02.269
So just keep that in mind as you're utilizing this,

143
00:06:02.269 --> 00:06:05.189
that the best results are going to come from something that

144
00:06:05.189 --> 00:06:06.790
gives a subtle fall off.

145
00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:08.990
And in many instances, I find that working

146
00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:13.069
with the landscape patch that utilizes

147
00:06:13.069 --> 00:06:17.589
just the rectangular fall off works really, really well.

148
00:06:17.589 --> 00:06:20.509
So here, again, we can see this working in action here

149
00:06:20.509 --> 00:06:21.029
for us.

150
00:06:21.029 --> 00:06:22.910
We're getting some nice fall off.

151
00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:25.589
And then, again, I can adjust this

152
00:06:25.589 --> 00:06:27.269
to meet the needs of my building.

153
00:06:27.269 --> 00:06:32.110
Or maybe I just come over here and move this down

154
00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:35.550
and maybe scale it up a little bit to, oops, undo that.

155
00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:36.990
And we'll just scale this back down.

156
00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:37.509
There we go.

157
00:06:37.509 --> 00:06:38.670
That works even better.

158
00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:39.189
All right.

159
00:06:39.189 --> 00:06:42.189
So that's how we would go about using those landscape

160
00:06:42.189 --> 00:06:45.509
patches and the landscape circle height

161
00:06:45.509 --> 00:06:49.870
patches to give us a really great foundation

162
00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:52.990
underneath a building that we are creating.
